1,024 x 4,096 weights, 0.1% of them outliers

  format                       bits/weight  weight error  output error
  unquantised (the reference)        16.00          0.0%          0.0%
  8-bit, one scale                    8.00         20.0%         20.0%
  4-bit, one scale                    4.00         79.6%         79.4%
  4-bit, a scale per 128              4.12         20.9%         20.9%
  4-bit, a scale per 32               4.50         12.2%         12.2%

One scale for the whole tensor must stretch to the largest outlier, so at four
bits nearly every ordinary weight rounds to zero. A scale per small group costs a
fraction of a bit and keeps the outliers from setting everyone else's precision.
A relative error on one matrix is not quality on a task; measure that on the eval
set, because whether 12% here costs anything depends on the model and the task.
